        {
          "id": "SP_DIPLASTRELLA_SPIRASTRELLOIDES_VAN_SOEST_2017",
          "name": "Diplastrella spirastrelloides Van Soest, 2017",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Diplastrella",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "(Fig. 106 a) Three fragments presumed to have originally been a single piece, thinly encrusting on sandy rubble. Thickness about 2 mm, lateral size several cm 2. Surface microhispid. Color in alcohol dirty white to pale beige. Consistency soft. Skeleton. Small groups of tylostyles erect on the substratum rising beyond a thick mass of microscleres. Spicules. (Figs 106 b – f) Tylostyles, diplasters. Tylostyles, slightly fusiform, with prominent rounded tyles, in a large size range, divisible in two-three overlapping categories, (1) largest (Figs 106 b, b 1), with prominent tyles, faintly curved especially in the upper half, 528 – 952 x 15.5 – 24 µm, (2) middle-sized (Figs 106 c, c 1), 324 – 486 x 12 – 14.5 µm, and (3) small (Figs 106 d, d 1), 267 – 374 x 5 – 12 µm, the latter tend to have slightly irregular tyles. Overall, tylostyles measure 268 – 542 – 952 x 5 – 15.4 – 24 µm. Diplasters with conical rays, in two shapes / size ranges, (1) large spheraster-like, slightly extended spicules (Fig. 106 e), 31 – 41.6 – 48 µm, and (2) small condensed, irregular, spiraster-like spicules (Figs 106 f), 11 – 18.3 – 26 µm",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:9052704",
          "authorship": "Van Soest",
          "yearPublished": "2017",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "1fc10e9e-d9b7-5af-9a2-3a9db8168c9cfc",
          "sourceIds": {
