        {
          "id": "SP_SPIRASTRELLA_ERYLICOLA_VAN_SOEST_2017",
          "name": "Spirastrella erylicola Van Soest, 2017",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Spirastrella",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "(Fig. 107 a) Thinly encrusting (<1 mm) on the holotype of Erylus rhabdocoronatus sp. nov. (RMNH Por. 9339). Microhispid. Lateral size about 1 cm 2. Color in alcohol orange-beige. No apparent openings. Skeleton. Single erect tylostyles, heads embedded in the sponge surface it encrusts, protruding through a thick crust of microscleres. Spicules. (Figs 107 b – c) Tylostyles, spirasters. Tylostyles (Figs 107 b, b 1), curved, with prominent heads and sharply pointed apices, 570 – 744 – 882 x 6 – 9.3 – 13 µm (heads 9 – 12.8 – 18 µm). Spirasters (Figs 107 c, c 1, c 2), in the form of singly curved asters, spines conical, compound; smaller forms are few, supposedly juvenile stages, including thinly spined forms, overall diameters 13 – 18.6 – 23 µm.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:8994644",
          "authorship": "Van Soest",
          "yearPublished": "2017",
          "children": [],
